Report su's failure to start the shell.
When ShellExecuteEx() failed, su exited with status 1 without a word,
so a declined UAC prompt, or a shell that Windows could not run, looked
the same as a shell that exited with status 1. Say that the user
cancelled the prompt, or that the program could not be executed and
why.

---
 loginutils/suw32.c |    6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/loginutils/suw32.c
+++ b/loginutils/suw32.c
@@ -138,6 +138,12 @@
 	info.nShow = SW_SHOWNORMAL;
 
 	if (!mingw_shell_execute(&info)) {
+		if (GetLastError() == ERROR_CANCELLED) {
+			bb_simple_error_msg("cancelled by user");
+		} else {
+			errno = err_win_to_posix();
+			bb_perror_msg("can't execute '%s'", bb_path);
+		}
 		ret = 1;
 		goto end;
 	}
